<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN MEN'S SINGLES RESULTS-DAY THREE.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN MEN'S SINGLES RESULTS-DAY THREE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Men's singles results on the third day of the French Open tennis tournament on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding.</p>
<p>Second round :</p>
<p>  Dick Norman (Sweden) beat Leander Paes (India)   6-3 6-2 3-6</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) beat Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) 6-4 6-2 4-6 7-5</p>
<p>Mark Philippoussis (Australia) beat Olivier Delaitre (France) 6-4 3-6 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>1-Pete Sampras (U.S.) beat Francisco Clavet (Spain) 6-1 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>5-Thomas Muster (Austria) beat Jeff Tarango (U.S.) 7-5 1-6 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Thierry Champion (France) beat Ramon Delgado (Paraguay) 6-2 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Nicolas Escude (France) beat Jonathan Stark (U.S.) 6-4 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Albert Portas (Spain) beat 9-Carlos Moya (Spain)  6-4 4-6 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Lionel Roux (France) beat Sebastien Lareau (Canada) 7-5 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Jan Siemerink (Netherlands) beat Salvador Navarro (Spain) 6-1 6-7 (1-7) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>3-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat Guillaume Raoux (France) 7-5 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Filip Dewulf (Belgium) beat Fernando Meligeni (Brazil) 6-4 6-2 3-6 1-6 6-3</p>
<p>Andrei Medvedev (Ukraine) beat Juan Albert Viloca (Spain) 6-4 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Cedric Pioline (France) beat Gaston Etlis (Argentina) 2-6 6-3 6-3 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>8-Alex Corretja (Spain) beat Jens Knippschild (Germany) 4-6 6-1 6-1 7-6 (10-8)</p>
<p>First round:</p>
<p>Frederic Fontang (France) beat Patrik Fredriksson (Sweden) 6-3 6-7 (6-8) 6-0 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>(ends men's results)</p>
</text>
